# Bug: a helper function in a test file may call a private name of the
# module, the checker lets it through, and the test fails at run time with
# a mangled name.
#
# Run from bugs/test_helper_reaches_private_name: kanso test m
#
# should: refuse `hidden` at check, as it refuses the same name in a test
#   constant ("error[name]: unknown name `hidden`", which `test_direct`
#   below gets when uncommented). Ruling 2026-10-12: a test file sees only
#   pub names.
# does: `test_through_helper ... FAILED` with "error[runtime]: unknown name
#   `~hidden`". The `~` is an internal spelling the author never wrote.

fn via n
  hidden n

test_through_helper = via 1 == 2

test_public = shown 1 == 2
